      "writtenOn": "2020-09-03T09:03:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried to use `installable` property before adding `is_uses_lib`, but it turns out that there are cases when `java_library` is `installable` but shouldn\u0027t be added as \u003cuses-library\u003e. I got multiple build errors caused by extra libraries being added to the \u003cuses-library\u003e list and abandoned the idea.",
      "parentUuid": "c4e1a343_ce2462d8",
      "revId": "21a73752054595c0e3cad5fa38dbedc2218998a2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0f3367e_0a290c8a",
        "filename": "java/app.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1887,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-03T10:11:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What determines whether something can be used in \u003cuses-library\u003e is whether there is a permissions.xml file that has a \u003clibrary\u003e entry for it. A lot of them are now created by java_sdk_library, but there are still many which are manually created - http://source/search?q\u003d%22%3Cpermissions%22%20%22%3Clibrary%22\u0026sq\u003dpackage:%5Eandroid$\n\nIdeally, we should migrate them to use java_sdk_library so that we can make sure that the API, which APPS may come to rely on, is properly managed. However, that is a large piece of work.",
      "parentUuid": "ffef4447_26aba10e",
      "revId": "21a73752054595c0e3cad5fa38dbedc2218998a2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
